      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Solar engineering sent 3 backpackers, an English electrician, an Irish labourer and another foreign helper, arriving at 11am 3 hours from their base with 2 houses to install on same day. They connected all 5.5 KW panels in parallel in only one string. Two strings are essential. When system was connected to my power it burnt out a pump and local electrician said turn off before it burns out the inverter as it hah 16 amp on the one line instead of near 8 amp as the maximum. After 2 years of trying to Get Solar Engineering to rewire my system properly, Office of Fair Trade tried to make SE fix their error, but were totally ignored, same response I received until they ceased to answer my calls or emails. I had to employ another registered solar electrician to re-wire all panels, add a second string with new switches, etc, at a cost greater than the original system. SE also left my shed roof leaking. Avoid this company if they still operate the way my system was installed.",
